  "solution": "Given:\n\nx + 1/x = 2√2\n\nFormula used:\n\nIf x + 1/x = n\n\nthen, x2 + 1/x2 = n2 - 2\n\nAnd (a + b)3 = a3 + b3 + 3ab (a + b)\n\nCalculation:\n\nx + 1/x = 2√2\n\n⇒ x2 + 1/x2 = (2√2)2 - 2\n\n⇒ x2 + 1/x2 = 6\n\nCubing both side we get\n\n⇒ (x2 + 1/x2)3 = 63\n\n⇒ x6 + 1/x6 + 3 (x2 × 1/x2) (x2 + 1/x2) = 63 \n\n⇒ x6 + 1/x6 + 3 × 1 × 6 = 63 \n\n⇒ x6 + 1/x6 = 63 - 3 × 6\n\n⇒ x6 + 1/x6 = 216 - 18\n\n⇒ x6 + 1/x6 = 198\n\n∴ The value of x6 + 1/x6 is 198.",
